From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Report a refused directory scan on ps5.

Every lookup that needs a case-insensitive search fails on this console. A
32-bit game asks for its imports exactly as its import table spells them --
USER32.dll, OLEAUT32.dll, PSAPI.DLL -- while the prefix holds user32.dll and
the rest in lower case, so the fstatat shortcut misses and the whole lookup
rests on pw_cwd_scan_directory. It answers no, GTA IV loses all 21 of its
imports, and loader_init ends the process with c0000135.

The two ways it can answer no are far apart. Either the directory was never
resolved (ret < 0: pw_cwd_resolve_at answers EBADF for a descriptor whose
path it does not track, and root_fd may well be one), or it was listed and
nothing matched (ret == 0), which would put the fault in the listing or in
match_dir_entry instead. Name which, with the directory and the wanted name,
and stop after 24 so the game's own opens cannot drown it.

Diagnostic only; no behaviour changes.
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
index ec35dea354..f4733ccb58 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
@@ -3177,6 +3177,27 @@ static NTSTATUS find_file_in_dir( int root_fd, char *unix_name, int pos, const W
     match.length = length;
     match.is_name_8_dot_3 = is_name_8_dot_3;
     ret = pw_cwd_scan_directory( root_fd, unix_name, match_dir_entry, &match, &flags );
+    /* ⚠ DIAGNOSTIC. Every lookup that needs this scan fails on this console,
+     * and nothing says which half is wrong. A 32-bit game asks for its imports
+     * exactly as its import table spells them -- USER32.dll, OLEAUT32.dll,
+     * PSAPI.DLL -- while the prefix holds user32.dll, so the fstatat shortcut
+     * above misses and everything then rests on this one call. It is answering
+     * no, and the only two ways it can are far apart: the directory could not
+     * be resolved at all (ret < 0, and pw_cwd_resolve_at answers EBADF for a
+     * descriptor whose path it is not tracking, which root_fd may well be), or
+     * it was read and no entry matched (ret == 0), which would put the fault in
+     * the listing or the comparison instead. Say which, with the directory and
+     * the name, and stop after a few so a game's own opens cannot drown it. */
+    {
+        static int reported;
+        if (ret <= 0 && reported < 24)
+        {
+            reported++;
+            ERR( "ps5 scan: dir %s want %s -> ret %d errno %d (root_fd %d)\n",
+                 debugstr_a(unix_name), debugstr_wn(name, length), ret,
+                 ret < 0 ? errno : 0, root_fd );
+        }
+    }
     if (ret < 0) return errno_to_status( errno );
     if (ret > 0)
     {
